// A many-out operation: well-formed as a description, unrepresentable as a cell.
//
// `divmod` returns a named result tuple. Stage-0 well-formedness accepts it —
// the bridge arity's three maps compose, with one monomial per output port,
// each reading every input — so this declaration produces no description
// diagnostic.
//
// The cell layer refuses it, and says so. A cell's consumer side is a linear
// spine whose operation frame `f(p̄; c)` carries exactly one return
// continuation, structurally rather than by a check, so there is no frame that
// delivers two results. The elaborator therefore declines the operation instead
// of narrowing it to its first output port and silently dropping `r`.
//
// Only `Zero`'s frame-defining cell reaches the store; `divmod` contributes
// nothing until the cell alphabet grows to carry named-port interfaces.
data NatDiv : Type {
  Zero : NatDiv;
  oper divmod(m : NatDiv, n : NatDiv) -> (q : NatDiv, r : NatDiv);
}

//@ mode: desc
//@ expect-desc-render: sign NatDiv { sort NatDiv : Type; oper divmod : (m : NatDiv, n : NatDiv) --> (q : NatDiv, r : NatDiv); }
//@ expect-desc-store-cells: 1
//@ expect-desc-cell-decline: operation `divmod` of `NatDiv` declares a many-out result
